<title>INDIA: Yield on Indian 91-day t-bill rises to 7.23 pct.</title>
<headline>Yield on Indian 91-day t-bill rises to 7.23 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said on Friday it set a cut-off price of 98.23 rupees at the five billion rupee weekly auction of 91-day treasury bills, down from 98.30 rupees at last week's auction.</p>
<p>Dealers said the yield worked out to 7.23 percent, up from 6.94 percent at the previous auction.  </p>
<p>				  Bids received	Amount (Rs. million)</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Competitive			   20		     3,223.3</p>
<p>Non-competitive			2		     2,500.0</p>
<p>					  ---		    -------</p>
<p>Total				   22		     5,723.3</p>
<p>					  ---		    -------</p>
<p>				   Bids allotted     Amount (Rs. million)</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Competitive			    9		    1,773.30</p>
<p>Non-competitive			2		    2,500.00</p>
<p>					  ---		    -------</p>
<p>Total				   11		    4,273.30</p>
<p>					  ---		    -------</p>
<p>Partial allotment		   Nil			---</p>
<p>Devolvement : Reserve Bank of India		     627.80</p>
<p>		  Primary dealers				98.90</p>
<p>Weighted average price - 98.26 rupees.</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------</p>
